        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lift only as far as needed",
            "`useContext` re-renders every consumer on change",
            "`useSyncExternalStore` for external mutable stores",
            "Drilling 2–3 levels is cheaper than context"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. What A Render Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An update re-renders that component + subtree",
            "Re-render means run the function, not touch DOM",
            "Reconciliation is roughly O(n) in elements",
            "Commits are expensive; React skips unchanged nodes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Memoization Has A Price",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An allocation, a deps array, a compare per render",
            "Plus memory retained for the cached value",
            "Not free, and not a default"
          ]
        }
      ],
