      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Memoize When",
          "items": [
            "The computation is genuinely expensive",
            "The value is a dep of an effect",
            "It is a prop to a `React.memo` child"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. React.memo, Defeated"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const Row = memo(RowImpl)",
            "<Row style={{ pad: 4 }} />  // ✗",
            "<Row onPick={() => go(id)}/> // ✗",
            "// new ref each render → re-render"
          ],
          "note": "shallow compare fails on inline props"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Colocate State"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Push state down to the ==smallest== owner",
            "The re-render radius shrinks with it",
            "Cheapest optimization — no memo needed",
            "Split setters in one handler still batch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Colocate, Then Measure",
          "text": "Most slowness is a wide re-render radius or an effect chain, not a missing useMemo. Shrink the radius, then profile."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. children As A Prop"
